1
00:01:30,566 --> 00:01:31,551
=Tigers Sniff the Rose=

2
00:01:31,551 --> 00:01:33,560
(Based on the novel of the same name by Yiren Kuikui)

3
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:38,900
=Episode 1=

4
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:49,660
(Huai Dynasty, Yingxiang 21, Spring)
(In the 21st year of Yingxiang,)

5
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:52,140
(Princess Danyang, Mu Wanyao,)

6
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:53,900
(visited Mount Lufu
to honor her late mother.)

7
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:54,820
(Caimei Ridge, Lingnan Circuit)

8
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:55,220
(On her way back,)

9
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:58,220
(she passed through Caimei Ridge
in Lingnan Circuit.)

10
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:03,420
(Something's wrong! Something's wrong!)

11
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:04,500
(Somebody, help!)

12
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:05,300
(A wheel spoke has snapped!)

13
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,140
(This road is terrible!)

14
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:07,020
(Grab a wooden pole to prop it up!)

15
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:07,900
(Coming!)

16
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:11,700
My lady, one of the carriage's
wheel spokes has broken.

17
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,740
(Mu Wanyao, Princess Danyang)

18
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:23,620
What a wretched place!

19
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:29,500
(Chunhua, Princess Danyang's Maid)

20
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:30,060
My lady.

21
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,580
Do you think there really are tigers
in these mountains?

22
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:35,340
This is Lingnan,

23
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,380
not Sheng'an.

24
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:37,820
Forget tigers and leopards.

25
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,860
Even spirits and monsters

26
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:41,180
wouldn't be surprising here.

27
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:43,660
My lady.

28
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:45,460
The carriage has a broken wheel spoke.

29
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:46,700
It'll take two hours to replace.

30
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:48,420
(Fang Tong, Princess Danyang's Guard)
We're still far from the relay station.

31
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,180
We can either
risk pressing on after dark

32
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,540
or spend the night here.

33
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:52,820
What would you prefer?

34
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:44,500
My lady!

35
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:45,940
There really are monsters here!

36
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:40,540
♪Moonlight shimmers upon the pond♪

37
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:44,660
♪Riding a bamboo horse
past the red pond♪

38
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:48,540
♪The water's too deep to cross♪

39
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:52,460
♪A maiden rows to fetch her love♪

40
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:56,420
♪She asks her sweetheart this and that♪

41
00:04:56,820 --> 00:05:00,340
♪When you leave again,
when will you be back?♪

42
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:05,780
You insolent rogue!

43
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,420
What are you staring at my lady for?

44
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,260
Are you heading across Caimei Ridge,
my lady?

45
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:14,620
What's it to you?

46
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:21,300
Another five li ahead,

47
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:22,420
you'll reach the official road.

48
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,180
Follow it east,

49
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:25,300
and you'll find a relay station.

50
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,060
Did anyone ask you for directions?

51
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:30,020
Besides,

52
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:32,300
how do I know
you're not just making it up?

53
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,460
You have a point, my lady.

54
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,020
You can never be too careful.

55
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:38,220
I'll be off, then.

56
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:39,620
Stop right there.

57
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:52,500
Where are you going?

58
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:53,700
Home.

59
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,260
No luggage,

60
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:58,420
and traveling on foot at dusk.

61
00:05:59,060 --> 00:05:59,780
Your home

62
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,260
must be somewhere in these mountains.

63
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:03,860
It is.

64
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:06,660
Then lead the way.

65
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:09,220
Wonderful, my lady!

66
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:11,220
We won't have to sleep out
in the wilderness tonight!

67
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:13,580
Well...

68
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:15,620
My home is rather small.

69
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:17,020
I'm afraid there isn't room
for so many guests.

70
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:21,260
You sure talk too much.

71
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:27,500
You're not afraid
I might be a liar anymore?

72
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:30,380
With that build of yours,

73
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:31,940
even if you meant me harm,

74
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:33,180
who could you possibly hurt?

75
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:55,980
You're a strange one.

76
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:57,620
It's not even dark yet.

77
00:06:58,580 --> 00:06:59,900
Why have you lit a torch already?

78
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,060
These woods are remote,

79
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:03,300
and we often run into wild animals.

80
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,140
Even by day, we carry torches
when we travel through the mountains.

81
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:07,460
You're a traveler from elsewhere,
aren't you, my lady?

82
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:10,740
What's your name?

83
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:11,980
My surname is Yan.

84
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,380
I'm the second child in my family.

85
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:17,860
Yan Shang.

86
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:20,220
Who else lives with you?

87
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:22,460
(Yan Shang)
My elderly father,

88
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:23,540
an older brother, and a younger sister.

89
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:25,380
And what should I call you, my lady?

90
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:28,300
There isn't a village or inn
in these mountains.

91
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:30,580
Why is yours the only family
living out here?

92
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:32,980
Are you refugees

93
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:34,140
or outlaws?

94
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:36,180
To tell you the truth, my lady,

95
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:37,620
when I first saw you,

96
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,500
surrounded by attendants
in the middle of nowhere,

97
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:40,660
a beautiful lady traveling alone,

98
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:42,980
I thought you might be a fox spirit
or a seductive ghost.

99
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:50,420
(What a temper this lady has.)

100
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:00,740
My lady.

101
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:01,980
My home is rather humble.

102
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:03,940
Are you sure you want to stay?

103
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:10,180
Guards!

104
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:13,700
Clear out

105
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:14,860
these two rooms.

106
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:15,620
I'll be using them.

107
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,540
Yes, my lady!

108
00:08:18,660 --> 00:08:18,980
(Over here!)

109
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:19,820
- (Here!)
- (Check over here!)

110
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:20,260
(Tear this place down!)

111
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:20,980
(Replace that stool!)

112
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:24,500
♪Dark clouds gather, rain's on its way♪

113
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,100
(Move aside! Make way! Clear the path!)

114
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:26,740
(Hurry up!)

115
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,100
(Move it! Faster!)

116
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:29,340
(Got it!)

117
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:33,740
Who are you people?

118
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,100
Where are you taking me?

119
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:36,900
There's a young lady here too?

120
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:39,420
What's so strange about that?

121
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:42,900
♪Oh, what a funny sight♪

122
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:44,180
My wine!

123
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,380
My wine!

124
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:50,420
♪Grandma wants it bland♪

125
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:51,380
Father!

126
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:52,260
Shang! Shang! Quick!

127
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:52,580
Father!

128
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,060
- Throw them out!
- Father! Father!

129
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:55,500
There's more wine! There's more wine!

130
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:57,580
Come on, get up!

131
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:58,300
Father!

132
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:00,540
Father!

133
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:01,660
Father!

134
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:02,980
Shang!

135
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:04,580
♪Clang-a-lang♪

136
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:07,140
(Yan Zhanzhi, Yan Shang's Father)

137
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:08,700
My wine!

138
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:09,060
Father!

139
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:10,020
Father!

140
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:10,900
Please, get up!

141
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:13,460
Shang!

142
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:16,180
I'll explain everything later.

143
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:16,660
My wine!

144
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:18,060
Father, there'll be more wine.

145
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,100
Just sit inside.

146
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:19,780
I'll handle this.

147
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:23,180
♪Grandpa digs up a loach♪

148
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:27,500
♪Oh, what a funny sight♪

149
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,500
Shang!

150
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:32,700
♪Grandpa wants it salty♪

151
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:35,940
♪Grandma wants it bland♪

152
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:40,980
♪They start a fight and smash the pot♪

153
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:44,460
♪Yi-ya-ha-do♪

154
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:47,580
♪Clang-a-lang, clang-a-lang♪
(Yan Dalang, Yan Shang's Older Brother)

155
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:48,220
Shang!

156
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:48,980
Father!

157
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:49,820
Run!

158
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:50,700
Run, Shang!

159
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:51,140
Brother!

160
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:51,980
(Yan Xiaozhou, Yan Shang's Sister)
Father, run!

161
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:53,020
- Brother!
- Bandits are in our house!

162
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:53,900
Let go of my brother!

163
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:54,220
Move!

164
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,420
Shang, run!

165
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:57,100
Xiaozhou, run!

166
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:57,580
Let him go!

167
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:57,980
Out of the way!

168
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,180
Who are you calling a bandit?

169
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:03,540
There's a woman bandit too!

170
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:04,980
Xiaozhou, run!

171
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:06,100
Run!

172
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:07,740
Brother! Brother!

173
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:08,780
She's not a bandit.

174
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:09,500
There are no bandits.

175
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:10,540
Father's fine.

176
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:11,540
We're all fine.

177
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:12,660
It's okay.

178
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:13,340
Yan Shang.

179
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,220
Does no one in your family

180
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:17,900
know how to treat people properly?

181
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:20,260
Is there no law in this world?

182
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:20,580
Father!

183
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:21,460
Father!

184
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:22,620
Father!

185
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:24,060
I am the law.

186
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:37,260
My lady.

187
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:38,940
My brother has a mental disability.

188
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:39,820
He meant no offense.

189
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,540
Could you please have mercy on him?

190
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:43,340
For a country bumpkin,

191
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:44,780
you know what's good for you.

192
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:50,500
- Shang is no country bumpkin!
- Brother!

193
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:52,220
- He's not a bumpkin!
- Brother!

194
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:52,620
Brother!

195
00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:53,020
Brother!

196
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:54,820
Stop it. Don't say another word!

197
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:55,980
- This is our house!
- Brother!

198
00:10:56,020 --> 00:10:56,340
Brother!

199
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:56,980
Let me go!

200
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:57,420
All right, all right.

201
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:58,580
He's not a bumpkin!

202
00:10:58,580 --> 00:10:59,780
- Brother!
- Go get changed.

203
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:00,460
This is our house!

204
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:01,100
- Brother!
- I'll keep an eye on him.

205
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:02,460
He's no country bumpkin!

206
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:03,740
I'll throw them all out!

207
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:04,780
Shang?

208
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:05,780
Let me go!

209
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:08,620
His name is Yan Shang.

210
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:11,620
I was only trying to help
with directions.

211
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:14,260
But they immediately ordered me
to lead them back to my house.

212
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:17,620
I take that road every day.

213
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:19,740
Never thought it'd bring so much trouble
to our door.

214
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:21,380
It's not your fault, brother.

215
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:22,660
If I'd run into her,

216
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:23,980
I'd have let her stay too.

217
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,300
That woman is clearly
used to getting her way.

218
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,660
She must be from
some prominent household.

219
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:33,420
Let's just hope they stay one night

220
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:34,620
and leave first thing tomorrow.

221
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:40,500
Brother, please don't argue
with them again.

222
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:42,180
Just listen to Shang, all right?

223
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:45,140
(You lot,)

224
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:46,780
(go get some proper tools!)

225
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:48,020
(Bring a horse over to help pull!)

226
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:52,140
Brother!

227
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:53,220
Brother!

228
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:54,260
Brother!

229
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:55,500
Brother!

230
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:56,780
You can't tear it down!

231
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:57,860
What are you doing?

232
00:11:58,380 --> 00:11:59,300
This is my house!

233
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:01,100
Your house is tiny and stuffy.

234
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:02,260
We'll suffocate in this heat!

235
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:03,740
- Widen the doorway,
- No!

236
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:04,380
knock down that wall,

237
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:05,460
- and we can finally catch a breeze.
- Don't touch anything!

238
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:10,300
We worked ourselves to the bone
building this house.

239
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:11,900
Don't worry.

240
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:15,660
This money

241
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,540
could build you eight or ten houses.

242
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:20,900
Carry on.

243
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:22,700
Don't touch my door!

244
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:24,940
Don't tear it down! Don't! Don't!

245
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:26,300
You bunch of bandits!

246
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,180
Stop it!

247
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:28,900
I'll fight you if you touch it!

248
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:29,780
Hands off!

249
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:33,340
So it's the heat that's troubling you,
my lady.

250
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:35,140
We haven't been good hosts.

251
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:37,460
But this house
is badly in need of repair.

252
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:38,780
If you tear down a wall,

253
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:39,780
it may not be safe to stay here.

254
00:12:40,140 --> 00:12:41,620
Wouldn't it be even better
if the house collapsed?

255
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:44,900
If it crushed the wicked woman like me,
who took over your house,

256
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:46,740
you'd be thrilled, wouldn't you?

257
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:47,940
You're our guest.

258
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:49,460
If you don't mind our humble home,

259
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:50,820
we'll do our best to treat you well.

260
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:51,940
Treat me well?

261
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:54,860
Fine.

262
00:12:55,660 --> 00:12:56,300
I want some wine.

263
00:12:56,900 --> 00:12:57,700
And make sure it's chilled.

264
00:12:57,940 --> 00:12:58,620
Lots of ice.

265
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:00,940
But you're a woman.

266
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:02,340
Women can drink too?

267
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:03,900
Brother!

268
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:04,860
What?

269
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:06,380
Is it against the law

270
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:08,340
for a woman to drink?

271
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:16,660
Just a moment, my lady.

272
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:18,620
Here.

273
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:21,620
Brother.

274
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:23,140
Brother.

275
00:13:23,620 --> 00:13:25,340
There are still a few jars
of your lychee wine left.

276
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:27,220
But I don't know where to get any ice.

277
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:28,300
We can't worry about that right now.

278
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:30,660
She's just tired and irritable
from the journey.

279
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:31,900
She's taking it out on our house.

280
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:32,860
So what do we do?

281
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:35,980
I'll fetch the wine.

282
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:01,740
Is that idiot still standing
by the door?

283
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:03,580
Still guarding his precious wall.

284
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:04,660
He's terrified we'll tear it down.

285
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:07,060
Those Yan brothers are quite a pair.

286
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:08,740
Yan Dalang is dumb as an ox.

287
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:09,700
Yan Shang

288
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:11,580
is as timid as a rabbit.

289
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:15,140
My lady.

290
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,340
Yan Shang has brought
some wine to cool you down.

291
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:21,540
He actually found some ice?

292
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:28,340
Where's the ice?

293
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:31,060
You've come a long way, my lady.

294
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:32,740
You must be tired.

295
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,460
This is our homemade fruit wine.

296
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:37,740
Chilled in water till it's cold as ice.

297
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:39,780
Just right to cool you down
and refresh you.

298
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:42,660
Cold as ice?

299
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:44,340
But it's still not ice.

300
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:46,660
Besides,

301
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:49,020
I've tasted dozens of fine wines
in Sheng'an,

302
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,780
even a few imported grape wines.

303
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:54,100
What could your homemade country wine

304
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:55,740
possibly have to offer?

305
00:14:58,220 --> 00:14:59,500
This wine is called Lingxi.

306
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:02,860
Legend has it that a white rhinoceros
dug the ground here with its horn,

307
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:04,100
and a spring burst forth.

308
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:06,380
From the spring grew a lychee tree,

309
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:08,540
bearing exquisite blossoms
and fragrant fruit.

310
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:15,060
This wine is made from the fruit
of that very tree.

311
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:16,860
Why not give it a try, my lady?

312
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:18,300
It's a shame

313
00:15:18,740 --> 00:15:19,860
you've come at the wrong time of year.

314
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:20,940
If you wait until summer,

315
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:22,780
you can taste fresh lychees too.

316
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,700
Yan Shang, you certainly know
how to spin a tale.

317
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:29,300
Pour it.

318
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:53,860
You're quite the smooth talker, Shang.

319
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:56,340
Why don't you have the first cup?

320
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:02,100
Truth be told, my lady,

321
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:03,860
I can't hold my liquor.

322
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:05,980
Even the smell makes me tipsy.

323
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:07,100
I'm afraid

324
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:09,020
I'd only spoil your enjoyment.

325
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:11,620
People who claim
they can't hold their liquor

326
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:13,180
usually drink like fish.

327
00:16:14,300 --> 00:16:15,500
Now that you've said that,

328
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:18,180
there's no way I'm letting you off.

329
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:21,100
Will you drink it yourself,

330
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:22,980
or shall I have someone
pour it down your throat?

331
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,940
Who knows
where this wine of yours came from?

332
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:26,060
And you expect my lady to drink it?

333
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:27,900
What if you've poisoned it?

334
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,500
If they managed to poison me,

335
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:32,380
their whole family would celebrate.

336
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:34,580
Yan Shang.

337
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,300
I don't think your wine

338
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:37,980
will cool me down.

339
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:40,540
It's only making my blood boil.

340
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,900
You really do ask the impossible,
my lady.

341
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:32,940
Impressive drinking!

342
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:41,380
My lady! The wine's poisoned!

343
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:54,940
He actually passed out drunk?

344
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:03,100
Who would've thought?

345
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:05,340
So that was one thing
he wasn't lying about.

346
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:14,700
Chunhua!

347
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,660
Since when do geckos make noise?

348
00:19:58,660 --> 00:19:59,820
(The moon here in Lingnan)

349
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:02,860
(seems so much clearer
than in Sheng'an.)

350
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,620
(If one could live like the Yan family,)

351
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:08,220
(all together in the mountains,)

352
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:09,900
(looking after one another,)

353
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:11,580
(content with simple food and drink...)

354
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:14,180
(Perhaps)

355
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:17,020
(that's a rare blessing in this world.)

356
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:36,060
(Yi Zhi consulted...)

357
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:47,580
It's the middle of the night.

358
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:48,660
What are you doing?

359
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:51,540
It's already the fourth watch.

360
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:53,140
Why are you still awake, my lady?

361
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,500
Your house is crawling with bugs!

362
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:58,820
Living in the mountains means sharing
your home with bugs and snakes.

363
00:20:59,740 --> 00:21:00,740
But it's not all bad.

364
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:03,420
Look.

365
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:06,260
Fireflies.

366
00:21:07,580 --> 00:21:08,460
Can you really see by that light?

367
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:10,140
With these fireflies,

368
00:21:10,460 --> 00:21:11,380
I save quite a bit on lamp oil.

369
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:13,380
I just have to catch new ones often
and replace them as needed,

370
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:15,140
so they don't die trapped inside.

371
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:22,180
(Yi Zhi consulted with Wu Xian.)

372
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:23,260
You can read?

373
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:25,540
What's that you're writing?

374
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:26,860
I'm copying a book.

375
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:28,740
Where's the book?

376
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:29,780
I've memorized it.

377
00:21:44,140 --> 00:21:45,060
My hand's getting sore.

378
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:49,460
Thank you.

379
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:14,060
When I was little,

380
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:16,740
my mother often took me out
to catch fireflies.

381
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:21,820
There are fireflies in Sheng'an too?

382
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:23,540
Of course.

383
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:31,940
You're so far from home, my lady.

384
00:22:32,420 --> 00:22:33,300
Your mother must be worried.

385
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:34,540
Perhaps you should

386
00:22:34,980 --> 00:22:35,940
- head home soon...
- That's none of your business!

387
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:46,900
If you want to stay out here
and enjoy the cool air,

388
00:22:47,980 --> 00:22:48,620
take this

389
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:50,140
to keep mosquitoes and other bugs away.

390
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:05,220
Why are the mosquitoes biting me
and not you?

391
00:23:06,340 --> 00:23:07,260
Probably because

392
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:09,100
you haven't burned any herbal incense.

393
00:23:09,860 --> 00:23:11,580
I've been burning storax incense
in my room.

394
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:13,620
I even hung up mosquito-repellent
sachets.

395
00:23:14,180 --> 00:23:16,620
Those won't work against Lingnan's
venomous insects.

396
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:19,300
You need a slow-burning cord
made from herbs you prepare yourself.

397
00:23:19,740 --> 00:23:20,660
Light one before bed.

398
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:22,100
Then why wasn't there one in my room?

399
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:25,940
Your attendants

400
00:23:26,500 --> 00:23:27,140
threw them all out.

401
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:40,820
Don't scratch it.

402
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:43,020
What is it?

403
00:23:52,780 --> 00:23:53,500
You've got a bug bite

404
00:23:54,340 --> 00:23:55,180
on your face.

405
00:24:00,860 --> 00:24:02,180
Try putting some
of this herbal balm on it.

406
00:24:02,660 --> 00:24:03,340
The swelling should go down soon.

407
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:13,180
It does smell a little unpleasant,

408
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:14,180
but give it a try.

409
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:22,300
A little to the left.

410
00:24:24,780 --> 00:24:25,100
To the right.

411
00:24:26,860 --> 00:24:27,220
Left.

412
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:28,660
Up a little, to the left.

413
00:24:28,860 --> 00:24:29,620
I can't see it!

414
00:24:29,900 --> 00:24:30,260
You do it.

415
00:24:30,580 --> 00:24:30,860
Here.

416
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:31,860
Hurry up.

417
00:25:13,020 --> 00:25:13,700
Th-there.

418
00:25:30,460 --> 00:25:31,180
What are you laughing at?

419
00:25:32,700 --> 00:25:33,220
Nothing.

420
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:35,220
My face

421
00:25:35,540 --> 00:25:36,860
must look ridiculous
after you put that on!

422
00:25:37,420 --> 00:25:37,820
No.

423
00:25:38,580 --> 00:25:38,900
Not at all.

424
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:40,380
Yan Shang!

425
00:25:40,900 --> 00:25:41,740
How dare you make fun of me!

426
00:25:42,300 --> 00:25:42,620
I...

427
00:25:46,460 --> 00:25:48,180
(Yi Zhi consulted with Wu Xian.)

428
00:25:49,940 --> 00:25:51,700
That rain came out of nowhere.

429
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:55,180
The rain here never gives you
any warning.

430
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:04,900
You should get out of the rain, my lady.

431
00:26:38,020 --> 00:26:40,940
(Duke of Zhao's Residence)

432
00:28:35,420 --> 00:28:36,740
Another sleepless night, my lady?

433
00:28:37,940 --> 00:28:38,620
I want to wash up and get dressed.

434
00:28:40,340 --> 00:28:41,020
Just a moment, my lady.

435
00:28:41,340 --> 00:28:42,180
I'll get everything ready.

436
00:29:03,420 --> 00:29:04,060
Everything's ready, my lady.

437
00:29:07,820 --> 00:29:08,420
(What's going on?)

438
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:10,140
(Why is everything wet?)

439
00:29:12,060 --> 00:29:13,220
My lady, I'll go take a look.

440
00:29:20,020 --> 00:29:20,500
My lady!

441
00:29:20,660 --> 00:29:21,140
My lady!

442
00:29:21,780 --> 00:29:22,260
My lady!

443
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:24,940
Somehow, your chest of cosmetics
got wet in the rain!

444
00:29:26,780 --> 00:29:28,580
(It's all because your roof leaked
in the middle of the night!)

445
00:29:30,060 --> 00:29:31,060
(You're just trying to bully us!)

446
00:30:02,220 --> 00:30:04,700
My lady, the Yan family's
roof was leaking!

447
00:30:05,020 --> 00:30:06,740
Did anyone force you to stay
in our leaky house?

448
00:30:07,660 --> 00:30:08,540
That's enough, brother!

449
00:30:09,380 --> 00:30:10,140
Serves you right!

450
00:30:10,140 --> 00:30:10,460
Brother!

451
00:30:10,540 --> 00:30:11,180
How dare you speak to me like that!

452
00:30:11,180 --> 00:30:12,180
- I... I'll say what I want!
- Brother!

453
00:30:12,180 --> 00:30:12,620
What's wrong with that?

454
00:30:12,740 --> 00:30:13,060
Brother!

455
00:30:13,260 --> 00:30:14,580
- Stop it, brother!
- (You!)

456
00:30:20,500 --> 00:30:20,940
Don't hurt him!

457
00:30:24,820 --> 00:30:25,300
Move aside!

458
00:30:25,700 --> 00:30:26,900
My brother hasn't done anything wrong!

459
00:30:27,340 --> 00:30:28,300
Why do you look ready to kill him?

460
00:30:28,940 --> 00:30:30,220
Who said I was going to
kill your brother?

461
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:32,340
I'm disciplining my own servants!

462
00:30:37,180 --> 00:30:38,860
You're going to attack someone
over some rouge?

463
00:30:39,260 --> 00:30:39,860
Is a servant's life

464
00:30:39,860 --> 00:30:41,380
worth less than a few pots of rouge?

465
00:30:41,820 --> 00:30:42,540
I said, get out of my way!

466
00:30:42,860 --> 00:30:43,500
Don't you understand?

467
00:30:47,740 --> 00:30:48,100
No!

468
00:30:57,460 --> 00:30:59,220
Thank you, my lady!
Thank you for sparing me!

469
00:30:59,700 --> 00:31:00,580
I entrusted that chest

470
00:31:01,180 --> 00:31:02,180
to you for safekeeping.

471
00:31:03,780 --> 00:31:04,620
Now that you've messed up,

472
00:31:05,580 --> 00:31:06,980
you think you can pin it on the Yans

473
00:31:07,540 --> 00:31:08,420
and I'll let you off?

474
00:31:09,940 --> 00:31:11,020
You bunch of fools!

475
00:31:11,460 --> 00:31:12,580
Do you take me for an idiot too?

476
00:31:12,700 --> 00:31:13,700
Forgive us, my lady!

477
00:31:13,700 --> 00:31:15,060
It was our fault!

478
00:31:15,060 --> 00:31:16,420
We were careless!

479
00:31:18,860 --> 00:31:19,700
Everyone responsible for this

480
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:21,740
report to Fang Tong for a whipping.

481
00:31:27,780 --> 00:31:28,620
I thought you were going to...

482
00:31:30,300 --> 00:31:31,700
You thought I was a spoiled tyrant

483
00:31:31,980 --> 00:31:32,820
who kills people on a whim?

484
00:31:39,300 --> 00:31:39,780
You're right.

485
00:31:41,180 --> 00:31:42,180
That's exactly the kind of person I am.

486
00:32:02,060 --> 00:32:02,660
My lady.

487
00:32:43,780 --> 00:32:44,340
I don't need your help.

488
00:32:44,900 --> 00:32:46,340
Rain can come out of nowhere
this time of year.

489
00:32:46,900 --> 00:32:47,740
I'll get an umbrella, then.

490
00:33:04,420 --> 00:33:04,820
Miss.

491
00:33:05,460 --> 00:33:07,060
Was that rouge very expensive?

492
00:33:08,900 --> 00:33:09,620
It's not about the money.

493
00:33:09,820 --> 00:33:10,500
It was precious to her.

494
00:33:11,220 --> 00:33:11,660
You wouldn't understand.

495
00:33:13,100 --> 00:33:13,460
You're right.

496
00:33:15,300 --> 00:33:16,820
I really don't understand
what happened this morning.

497
00:33:17,540 --> 00:33:18,700
Could you help me make sense of it?

498
00:33:19,340 --> 00:33:20,020
That rouge...

499
00:33:20,380 --> 00:33:21,860
She takes it everywhere she goes.

500
00:33:22,340 --> 00:33:23,220
She can barely bring herself to use it.

501
00:33:23,700 --> 00:33:24,540
And now it's all ruined.

502
00:33:24,900 --> 00:33:25,980
You men would never understand.

503
00:33:32,820 --> 00:33:33,660
Is that all there is to it?

504
00:33:37,380 --> 00:33:38,460
The rest is none of your business.

505
00:33:45,020 --> 00:33:46,740
You'd better hurry and apologize
to my lady.

506
00:33:47,020 --> 00:33:48,300
She's really furious today.

507
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:52,460
Thank you for the advice.

508
00:33:53,060 --> 00:33:54,940
But she's still angry now.

509
00:33:56,100 --> 00:33:57,780
Perhaps I should prepare
a generous gift by way of apology

510
00:33:58,180 --> 00:33:59,820
and present it when she leaves,

511
00:34:00,180 --> 00:34:00,980
as a farewell gift too.

512
00:34:01,500 --> 00:34:02,180
I just wonder...

513
00:34:02,780 --> 00:34:03,980
When is she planning to leave?

514
00:34:06,260 --> 00:34:06,780
Well...

515
00:34:08,100 --> 00:34:08,980
I'll ask her for you.

516
00:34:09,460 --> 00:34:09,900
Thank you.

517
00:34:11,020 --> 00:34:11,420
Yan Shang!

518
00:34:12,100 --> 00:34:12,980
Listen carefully!

519
00:34:13,980 --> 00:34:15,340
I love traveling far from home,

520
00:34:15,900 --> 00:34:17,180
and I love staying in your shabby house!

521
00:34:17,580 --> 00:34:18,940
I'll stay as long as I please!

522
00:34:20,100 --> 00:34:21,260
Cross me again,

523
00:34:21,740 --> 00:34:23,380
and you'll get far worse than a slap!

524
00:34:24,540 --> 00:34:25,340
I might even

525
00:34:25,860 --> 00:34:27,300
tear your entire house to the ground.

526
00:34:29,780 --> 00:34:30,620
Bring me another jar of wine.

527
00:34:44,380 --> 00:34:45,300
After all that,

528
00:34:45,620 --> 00:34:47,420
I doubt she'll leave that easily now.

529
00:34:48,620 --> 00:34:49,780
With a temper like hers,

530
00:34:49,980 --> 00:34:50,940
if she stays much longer,

531
00:34:51,300 --> 00:34:52,620
there could be serious trouble.

532
00:34:54,580 --> 00:34:56,060
Just who is this woman?

533
00:35:03,140 --> 00:35:03,580
Xiaozhou.

534
00:35:04,180 --> 00:35:05,100
I need to get to the local school.

535
00:35:05,580 --> 00:35:06,340
Our brother can be rather careless.

536
00:35:06,900 --> 00:35:08,420
Please keep a close eye on things
at home.

537
00:35:09,100 --> 00:35:09,420
Sure.

538
00:35:18,220 --> 00:35:21,180
(Diligent Study, Steadfast Practice)
A gentleman follows the Way,

539
00:35:22,020 --> 00:35:23,780
but may give up halfway.

540
00:35:24,740 --> 00:35:27,260
I could never bring myself to stop.

541
00:35:28,140 --> 00:35:30,620
A gentleman holds fast
to the Middle Way.

542
00:35:31,460 --> 00:35:34,580
Though he lives in obscurity,

543
00:35:34,980 --> 00:35:36,420
he has no regrets.

544
00:35:37,060 --> 00:35:40,220
Only a sage can achieve this.

545
00:35:42,540 --> 00:35:43,260
In my opinion,

546
00:35:43,860 --> 00:35:45,193
(Learning without thought is labor lost;
thought without learning is perilous.)

547
00:35:45,194 --> 00:35:45,740
Whether the Way prevails or not,

548
00:35:46,260 --> 00:35:47,740
a man born into this world should

549
00:35:48,060 --> 00:35:48,860
serve the people and keep the peace,

550
00:35:49,020 --> 00:35:50,020
be loyal to his ruler and country.

551
00:35:50,500 --> 00:35:51,420
That is what a true man should do.

552
00:35:51,580 --> 00:35:53,060
And you, Shang?

553
00:35:53,580 --> 00:35:55,140
What do you think?

554
00:35:55,540 --> 00:35:57,580
Master, I have no desire
to pursue strange, obscure ways.

555
00:35:58,060 --> 00:35:59,220
Nor could I live in seclusion,
unknown to the world.

556
00:36:00,220 --> 00:36:01,340
Those things feel far beyond me.

557
00:36:01,820 --> 00:36:03,060
They're not beyond you.

558
00:36:03,500 --> 00:36:06,860
You simply haven't found
your own Way yet.

559
00:36:18,540 --> 00:36:22,020
♪Moonlight shimmers upon the pond♪

560
00:36:22,700 --> 00:36:26,140
♪Riding a bamboo horse
past the red pond♪

561
00:36:26,620 --> 00:36:30,020
♪The water's too deep to cross♪

562
00:36:30,460 --> 00:36:33,900
♪A maiden rows to fetch her love♪

563
00:36:35,460 --> 00:36:36,180
(Diligent Study, Steadfast Practice)
(Yan Shang, we're off!)

564
00:36:36,180 --> 00:36:36,540
(Heading home.)

565
00:36:36,620 --> 00:36:37,060
(We'll take our leave.)

566
00:36:37,060 --> 00:36:38,460
Yan Shang, have you finished
copying my book?

567
00:36:38,820 --> 00:36:39,260
All done.

568
00:36:41,220 --> 00:36:42,660
Yan Shang,
have you finished my policy essay?

569
00:36:43,100 --> 00:36:43,900
Take a look and see if it's all right.

570
00:36:44,420 --> 00:36:44,860
No need.

571
00:36:45,140 --> 00:36:46,260
Everything you ghostwrite is excellent.

572
00:36:47,100 --> 00:36:48,220
Here. Your payment.

573
00:36:48,740 --> 00:36:49,140
- (Let's go.)
- (Go.)

574
00:36:50,220 --> 00:36:50,500
(Let's go!)

575
00:36:50,940 --> 00:36:51,380
Yan Shang.

576
00:36:51,700 --> 00:36:52,500
I have to go now.

577
00:36:52,780 --> 00:36:54,300
Mind clearing my desk for me?

578
00:36:54,500 --> 00:36:54,780
Sure.

579
00:36:57,340 --> 00:36:58,820
Liu Wenji, what'd you hit me for?

580
00:36:58,980 --> 00:37:00,500
Shang works for the local school,

581
00:37:00,660 --> 00:37:01,620
not for you.

582
00:37:01,860 --> 00:37:02,780
You've got plenty of servants at home.

583
00:37:02,940 --> 00:37:03,900
Why not have them clean up after you?

584
00:37:06,460 --> 00:37:10,340
(Liu Wenji, Son of the Shaozhou Prefect,
Yan Shang's Classmate)

585
00:37:10,980 --> 00:37:11,380
Wenji.

586
00:37:12,140 --> 00:37:12,900
It's no big deal.

587
00:37:13,180 --> 00:37:13,900
No need to get upset.

588
00:37:15,380 --> 00:37:16,460
(Diligent Study, Steadfast Practice)
The more accommodating you are,

589
00:37:16,660 --> 00:37:17,980
the more they'll walk all over you.

590
00:37:19,180 --> 00:37:19,940
I promise you,

591
00:37:20,220 --> 00:37:22,060
even if you beat them all up tomorrow,

592
00:37:22,620 --> 00:37:23,140
as long as I'm around,

593
00:37:23,500 --> 00:37:25,260
you can still work and study here.

594
00:37:25,780 --> 00:37:26,180
All right.

595
00:37:26,780 --> 00:37:28,420
Then I'll beat them all up tomorrow.

596
00:37:30,140 --> 00:37:31,180
Even without me,

597
00:37:31,420 --> 00:37:32,580
they'd never let you leave.

598
00:37:33,020 --> 00:37:34,460
What would anyone do without you?

599
00:37:41,620 --> 00:37:43,020
Yesterday, I was copying
official documents for my father.

600
00:37:43,300 --> 00:37:45,820
I read this month's latest copy
of the court bulletin.

601
00:37:48,100 --> 00:37:49,460
Anything major happening lately?

602
00:37:49,940 --> 00:37:50,660
Nothing major.

603
00:37:51,020 --> 00:37:52,580
But there was one rather interesting
little story.

604
00:37:54,140 --> 00:37:55,660
Apparently, Princess Danyang
is a devoted daughter.

605
00:37:55,980 --> 00:37:58,260
She traveled all the way
from Sheng'an to Mount Lufu

606
00:37:58,380 --> 00:38:00,340
to pray for the late Empress
and perform rites for her soul.

607
00:38:00,820 --> 00:38:01,660
By my reckoning,

608
00:38:02,140 --> 00:38:03,020
she should be in Lingnan by now.

609
00:38:03,420 --> 00:38:05,900
Every prefecture along the route
has prepared a grand welcome.

610
00:38:07,100 --> 00:38:08,140
After all, she's now

611
00:38:08,580 --> 00:38:10,700
His Majesty's only beloved daughter.

612
00:38:11,580 --> 00:38:12,580
But guess what?

613
00:38:13,940 --> 00:38:14,420
What?

614
00:38:15,420 --> 00:38:17,020
Not a single prefecture has seen her.

615
00:38:18,220 --> 00:38:19,180
Strange, isn't it?

616
00:38:22,140 --> 00:38:23,780
(So she's Princess Danyang.)

617
00:38:26,820 --> 00:38:27,780
(Then forgive me, Your Highness.)

618
00:38:27,780 --> 00:38:29,020
(Merit Through the Ages)

619
00:38:29,020 --> 00:38:30,020
(Our humble home)

620
00:38:30,620 --> 00:38:32,340
(is no place for someone
of your royal standing.)

621
00:38:33,220 --> 00:38:35,020
(And my family can't afford
any more trouble.)

622
00:38:35,020 --> 00:38:40,980
(Santu County Office)

623
00:38:40,980 --> 00:38:41,660
What do you want?

624
00:38:43,300 --> 00:38:43,820
Sir,

625
00:38:44,500 --> 00:38:46,100
something strange happened to me today.

626
00:38:46,780 --> 00:38:47,580
After giving it some thought,

627
00:38:47,980 --> 00:38:49,020
I decided I should report it
to the magistrate.

628
00:38:49,580 --> 00:38:50,580
What's so strange about it?

629
00:38:51,940 --> 00:38:53,380
I was passing through Caimei Ridge today

630
00:38:53,780 --> 00:38:54,660
when I came across a carriage.

631
00:38:55,260 --> 00:38:57,700
There was a lady inside who claimed
to be Princess Danyang.

632
00:38:58,260 --> 00:38:59,100
(Chen Da, Santu County Bailiff)
She'd gotten lost in the mountains

633
00:38:59,460 --> 00:39:00,260
and was looking for someone
from the prefectural office.

634
00:39:00,780 --> 00:39:02,180
(Merit Through the Ages)

635
00:39:02,180 --> 00:39:03,020
Princess Danyang?

636
00:39:03,660 --> 00:39:04,620
Are you sure you heard that right?

637
00:39:06,420 --> 00:39:07,740
I think that's what I heard.

638
00:39:08,700 --> 00:39:09,420
(Zhang Renjing,
Captain of the Shence Army)

639
00:39:09,420 --> 00:39:09,980
This journey

640
00:39:11,540 --> 00:39:12,460
has completely worn me out.

641
00:39:14,940 --> 00:39:16,180
I'm lucky you've taken
such good care of me.

642
00:39:17,060 --> 00:39:18,540
Oh, think nothing of it!

643
00:39:19,020 --> 00:39:20,420
Once you arrive in Sheng'an, Captain,

644
00:39:20,780 --> 00:39:22,260
and catch Lord Yu's eye,

645
00:39:22,540 --> 00:39:25,060
you'll have a brilliant career
ahead of you!

646
00:39:25,500 --> 00:39:26,860
Oh, I wouldn't count on that.

647
00:39:27,980 --> 00:39:29,900
Lord Yu is a man of great stature!

648
00:39:30,540 --> 00:39:31,660
(Zheng Chengqing, County Magistrate)
If he even recognizes me,

649
00:39:31,980 --> 00:39:33,740
I'd consider myself blessed
beyond belief.

650
00:39:34,300 --> 00:39:35,380
You're too modest, Captain.

651
00:39:41,340 --> 00:39:42,060
What do you think you're doing?

652
00:39:42,100 --> 00:39:42,980
Can't you see the captain's here?

653
00:39:43,660 --> 00:39:46,220
I've found a lead on Princess Danyang's
whereabouts.

654
00:39:47,940 --> 00:39:48,580
Are you certain?

655
00:39:49,060 --> 00:39:50,020
Absolutely certain!

656
00:39:50,300 --> 00:39:52,060
Someone spotted her at Caimei Ridge!

657
00:39:53,180 --> 00:39:53,580
Your Honor,

658
00:39:54,260 --> 00:39:55,980
once you find the princess tomorrow,

659
00:39:56,300 --> 00:39:58,300
invite her to stay at our county office.

660
00:39:58,860 --> 00:40:00,820
Then the prefect himself will surely
pay us a visit!

661
00:40:02,940 --> 00:40:04,420
Gather a troop of men at once.

662
00:40:04,580 --> 00:40:05,340
Prepare some lavish gifts.

663
00:40:05,660 --> 00:40:07,300
I'll pay my respects
to Her Highness myself tomorrow.

664
00:40:07,540 --> 00:40:07,980
Yes, sir! Right away!

665
00:40:10,500 --> 00:40:11,380
Come, Captain. Another drink!

666
00:40:11,940 --> 00:40:12,780
No more, no more.

667
00:40:13,460 --> 00:40:14,180
I should get going.

668
00:40:14,780 --> 00:40:16,020
Can't afford to fall behind schedule.

669
00:40:16,620 --> 00:40:17,100
Of course, of course!

670
00:40:17,500 --> 00:40:18,340
Watch your step.

671
00:40:18,340 --> 00:40:18,860
All right, all right.

672
00:40:19,780 --> 00:40:20,260
No need to see me out.

673
00:40:20,740 --> 00:40:21,180
Okay.

674
00:40:21,180 --> 00:40:21,860
No need to come any farther.

675
00:40:56,020 --> 00:40:58,020
(Santu County Office
Merit Through the Ages)

676
00:41:10,340 --> 00:41:12,340
(Santu County Office)

677
00:41:16,140 --> 00:41:17,220
Out of my way!

678
00:41:19,660 --> 00:41:19,980
(Santu County Office)
Get lost!

679
00:41:30,340 --> 00:41:31,980
(Santu County Office)

680
00:41:33,500 --> 00:41:33,780
Go!

681
00:41:38,220 --> 00:41:40,300
(Merit Through the Ages)

682
00:41:48,700 --> 00:41:49,580
(It's him.)

683
00:41:53,140 --> 00:41:55,300
(He's actually still alive.)

684
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:04,740
(Next Episode Preview)

685
00:42:04,980 --> 00:42:05,740
I want to get out of here.

686
00:42:06,140 --> 00:42:07,020
She's an honored guest from Sheng'an.

687
00:42:07,020 --> 00:42:08,220
She could give me that chance.

688
00:42:08,460 --> 00:42:09,860
You think groveling at her feet

689
00:42:09,860 --> 00:42:11,060
will send you soaring through the ranks?

690
00:42:11,500 --> 00:42:12,580
Better than living like you,

691
00:42:12,860 --> 00:42:14,540
hiding in this wretched backwater
your whole life,

692
00:42:14,540 --> 00:42:15,980
shutting out the world like a coward!

693
00:42:16,340 --> 00:42:17,700
Have you no shame?

694
00:42:21,120 --> 00:42:24,413
♪Be the ferry
where you wait for the sun♪

695
00:42:27,098 --> 00:42:32,014
♪Be the blue silk
that catches your tears♪

696
00:42:34,208 --> 00:42:40,053
♪Be the sleeve we held,
worn by dust and years♪

697
00:42:40,553 --> 00:42:45,779
♪Let's conspire to grow old together♪

698
00:42:48,548 --> 00:42:53,339
♪Let me be a captive beast
bound by the same lock as you♪

699
00:42:54,175 --> 00:43:00,254
♪Through trails of mud and blood;
let grief drown in your eyes♪

700
00:43:02,055 --> 00:43:05,205
♪Soar with the wind;
plunge into hellfire as one♪

701
00:43:05,205 --> 00:43:06,853
♪Burning bright as a song♪

702
00:43:06,905 --> 00:43:10,629
♪See how roses and green bamboo enchant♪

703
00:43:11,007 --> 00:43:15,673
♪Be the vow I make with all my heart♪

704
00:43:16,292 --> 00:43:20,333
♪If we say forever,
then forever it shall be♪

705
00:43:20,824 --> 00:43:22,939
♪Not a single hour less♪

706
00:43:22,979 --> 00:43:29,925
♪However deep the snow,
I'll wait if you're there♪

707
00:43:30,688 --> 00:43:34,141
♪We'll be gods above,
or wandering souls♪

708
00:43:34,321 --> 00:43:37,466
♪In heaven or the underworld,
you're all I need♪

709
00:43:37,905 --> 00:43:44,542
♪If we can stay, let's return
to the village of our first meeting♪

710
00:43:44,939 --> 00:43:49,453
♪May time be free of fear and pain;
boats rock, lights fade, seasons turn♪

711
00:43:49,491 --> 00:43:51,960
♪You're the only one I need♪

712
00:43:52,164 --> 00:43:59,051
♪Sharp winds or fierce rain,
nothing can break us♪

713
00:43:59,363 --> 00:44:02,634
♪Be mine in this world;
be mine in this life♪

714
00:44:02,939 --> 00:44:06,112
♪My last untouched innocence♪

715
00:44:06,436 --> 00:44:09,862
♪If only we could return
to the village where we first met♪

716
00:44:10,095 --> 00:44:13,320
♪Stay by me; help me forget
the frozen dream of last night♪

717
00:44:13,651 --> 00:44:20,447
♪Fireflies glow, flowers kiss our lips;
just us, through dawn and dusk♪

718
00:44:20,816 --> 00:44:25,382
♪May time be free of fear and pain;
boats rock, lights fade, seasons turn♪

719
00:44:25,429 --> 00:44:27,767
♪You're the only one I need♪

720
00:44:27,998 --> 00:44:34,833
♪By your side, through joy and pain,
is that eternity?♪

721
00:44:35,182 --> 00:44:36,800
♪Till fireworks flood the town♪

722
00:44:36,930 --> 00:44:38,726
♪Till the lake is still and clear♪

723
00:44:39,083 --> 00:44:42,100
♪You're the only one I need♪

724
00:44:42,140 --> 00:44:43,467
(No animals were harmed
or mistreated in production.)
